    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule for `POST /api/owners`: creating an owner is now rejected with **409 Conflict** when the target city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions, I added:\n\n1. **`RequireCityCapacity.java`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a pipeline step that counts existing owners whose (normalized) city matches the request's city and throws `CityAtCapacityException` when the count reaches 50. City comparison uses the same trim/collapse-whitespace/lower-case normalization the rest of the pipeline uses.\n\n2. **`CityAtCapacityException.java`** \u2014 a checked exception (extends `Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n\n3. **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds `409` with body `{\"errors\":[\"city\"]}`, mirroring the existing `DuplicateTelephone`/`DuplicateHousehold` 409 handlers.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** `officefloor/escalation/...CityAtCapacityException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **Wired the step** into `owners.POST.yml` as `cityCapacity` (with `govern: [ transaction ]`), placed after the uniqueness checks and before `build`.\n\nBoth the new acceptance test (`coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity`) and the full test suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures).",
